# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values for local development.
# Do not commit `.env.local`. Only non-secret placeholders belong in this file.

# Public base URL of the app (used for absolute links / metadata).
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Human-readable environment label shown in non-production builds.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave DATABASE_URL UNSET for local development: the app and the db:* scripts
# use an embedded PostgreSQL (PGlite) stored in ./.pglite (git-ignored).
# Set it to a real PostgreSQL server for staging/production, then run
# `npm run db:migrate` in the deploy pipeline (migrations never run at request time).
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/intra

# Optional: override the embedded PGlite data directory.
# PGLITE_DATA_DIR=./.pglite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operator authentication
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated "label:secret" pairs. An operator presents the secret in the
# `x-operator-key` header. Required to verify/activate a route (PATCH
# /api/routes/:id/status -> ACTIVE) and to record a quote response.
# With none configured, no request can act as an operator.
# OPERATOR_API_KEYS=alice:change-me-locally,bob:change-me-too

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web push  (milestone 7 phase C)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Self-generated VAPID keypair — NOT from any third party, no account, no cost.
#   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# Generate a SEPARATE pair per environment. The PRIVATE key is a secret: never
# commit it, only set it in the deployment's env. With any of the three unset,
# push is UNAVAILABLE and the app falls back to in-app notifications only —
# nothing breaks.
#
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY            the app-server identity the browser subscribes with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY  same value, exposed to the client (optional — the
#                              client also reads it from /api/push/config)
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY          SERVER-ONLY secret. Never NEXT_PUBLIC_, never logged.
# VAPID_SUBJECT              a contact the push services can reach you at:
#                           mailto:you@domain  or  https://your-site
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Celo x402 agent payments  (see docs/PAYMENTS.md — ADR-004, ADR-011)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Leave X402_API_KEY unset and the
# quote endpoint returns PAYMENT_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE — no 402, no fabricated
# settlement, receipt, or tx hash. Free routes and the buyer web flow are
# unaffected. A malformed X402_NETWORK / X402_ASSET / X402_ATTRIBUTION_TAG is
# logged once and degrades to the same unavailable state — it never crashes the
# quote workflow.
#
# X402_API_KEY: the metering key from the dashboard at https://x402.celo.org
#   (connect wallet -> Create API key -> sign; shown once). Gates POST /settle.
# X402_API_KEY=
#
# X402_NETWORK: CAIP-2 id. Default eip155:42220 (Celo Mainnet).
#   Celo Sepolia is eip155:11142220.
# X402_NETWORK=eip155:42220
#
# X402_ASSET: USDC (default) or USDT. USDT is mainnet-only.
# X402_ASSET=USDC
#
# X402_FACILITATOR_URL: optional override. Defaults per network:
#   mainnet  https://api.x402.celo.org
#   sepolia  https://api.x402.sepolia.celo.org
# X402_FACILITATOR_URL=
#
# X402_ATTRIBUTION_TAG: the ERC-8021 `celo_...` tag from official hackathon
#   registration (/^celo_[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_-]{2,62}$/). Only set once you
#   have it — it is recorded on receipts. A value that does not match the shape
#   is ignored with a logged warning, never recorded.
# X402_ATTRIBUTION_TAG=

# The task-level spending cap ($0.05) is a hard product rule, not an env var.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Buyer-agent model layer  (ADR-019, milestone 3)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY. The LLM sits ABOVE the deterministic orchestration: it does
# intent understanding, provider selection and replanning. Budget caps, quote
# expiry, eligibility, the human approval gate and every mutating tool stay
# deterministic. With NO key set the agent runs fully deterministically — the
# `/agent` page and `/api/agent/*` still work, just without model reasoning.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: from https://console.anthropic.com. Never prefix with
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_, never log it, never send it to the browser.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# AGENT_MODEL_PROVIDER: "anthropic" (default when a key is present) | "mock"
#   (deterministic stand-in, no credits — used by tests) | "off" (force the
#   deterministic path). Unset + no key ⇒ deterministic.
# AGENT_MODEL_PROVIDER=
#
# AGENT_MODEL: optional model id override. Default: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001.
# AGENT_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Attestation / chain environment  (ADR-018)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verified 2026-09-01 by direct eth_getCode: EAS, SchemaRegistry and both
# ERC-8004 registries are deployed on Celo MAINNET and have NO CODE on Celo
# Sepolia. There is no testnet to develop attestations against, so staging runs
# a clearly-labelled local mock and never claims to be on-chain.
#
# NETWORK_ENV: staging (default) | production.
#   staging    -> attestation mode "mock". Nothing is written to any chain.
#   production -> attestation mode "celo-mainnet", but ONLY with a signer set;
#                 without one it degrades to "mock" rather than fabricating.
# NETWORK_ENV=staging
#
# RPC_URL: defaults to https://forno.celo.org in production.
# RPC_URL=
#
# Contract overrides. Leave unset to use the verified addresses in
# src/features/attestation/chain.ts.
# EAS_CONTRACT=
# SCHEMA_REGISTRY=
# ERC8004_IDENTITY=
# ERC8004_REPUTATION=
#
# ATTESTATION_SIGNER_KEY: SERVER-ONLY private key for the agent wallet that
#   signs EAS attestations and ERC-8004 calls. Never commit it, never prefix
#   with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never log it. Use a dedicated wallet holding only gas.
# ATTESTATION_SIGNER_KEY=
